  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a sixteen-song set at the second Fast Forward festival in Nijmegen, Netherlands, on April 22, 1995 [1]. This recording, taped by Gregor Kessler and transferred by notasfarwest, is the only available audio of the show and lasts forty-five minutes [1]. The band, consisting of John and Rachel, opened with a cover of The Chiffons’ “One Fine Day,” which is the earliest archived performance of that track [1][2]. They followed with “Downtown Seoul” and “Going to Jamaica,” the latter also marking its first appearance in the archive [1][2]. The setlist included “Going to Georgia,” “The Recognition Scene,” and “Going to Palestine” [1]. “Song for Cleomenes” is notable as the only archived performance of that song, while “Alabama Nova” is one of only three archived performances [1][2]. The group played “Prana Ferox” and “Alpha Double Negative: Going to Catalina,” the latter being a first in the archive [1][2]. “Then the Letting Go” is rare, with only two archived performances, and “Seeing Daylight” is also a first in the archive [1][2]. The set continued with “Some Swedish Trees” [1]. They concluded with a cover of “The Sign” and “Going to Scotland,” which is the earliest archived performance of that song [1][2]. This is the third show in the archive’s collection for the band, following a performance at The Chameleon in January 1995 [2].",
